# Doc reading and writing

## Reading docs

- Project documentation lives under **`ai-docs/`** in **`.md`** or **`.txt`** format. Use **`README.md`** (root) as the index to see what doc is where.
- **`ai-docs/architecture/`** — system design, APIs, dev guide, implementation details.
- **`ai-docs/features/`** — feature specs, flows, demos, user/quick-start guides.
- **`ai-docs/decisions/`** — analyses, issue writeups, verification checklists, revalidation notes.
- When answering questions about the codebase or features, read from `ai-docs/` when relevant (e.g. DEVELOPMENT.md for patterns, feature docs for behaviour).

## Writing docs

- **Do not** add new **`.md`** or **`.txt`** documentation files at the project root (only `README.md` stays there). Leave dependency/config `.txt` files (e.g. `requirements.txt`) in their current locations.
- Add new docs under **`ai-docs/`** as **`.md`** or **`.txt`**, in the folder that matches the content:
  - **`ai-docs/architecture/`** — how the system is built (APIs, dev setup, implementation notes).
  - **`ai-docs/features/`** — what a feature does, flows, demos, guides.
  - **`ai-docs/decisions/`** — why something was done, analyses, issue notes, checklists.
- After adding a doc, update **root `README.md`**: add one line in the right category with the filename and a short description.
